FORM: KIN-FORCE-DERIVED -- a winding on a strand feels F_kink = 2 pi c_L eps' from the registered lock; the chain obeys it with the
      sine-Gordon mass to 1 pct. The mesh has a q E along the strand, built from registered objects only.
FORM: KIN-DRIFTS (with the loss identified) -- above a threshold below 1e-8 the winding accelerates relativistically to ~0.5 c_t and then
      reaches a terminal velocity of about 0.7 c_t at w = 2 (higher at w = 2.8), the excess work radiated as phonons into the strand.
      This is a steady drift at the registered couplings, but at the torsion-speed scale, not the mm/s of a copper wire; the loss is the
      strand's own discreteness, an instrument-class property of the registered chain (FND-STRAND-002's node spacing).
